# Source modules whose filenames collide with a global secrets-ignore pattern.
#
# A machine-level excludesFile (e.g. ~/.config/git/ignore) that blocks
# `credentials.*` / `secrets.*` to stop real secret files being committed is
# good hygiene, and it has a false positive here: `credentials.service.ts` is
# ORDINARY SOURCE. Without these negations `git add <dir>` skips those files
# silently — no warning, no error — and the commit lands with `app.module.ts`
# importing a module that is not in the repository. That happened once already
# (issue #115); it passes locally, because the files are on disk, and only
# fails for CI and for the next person to clone.
#
# Repo .gitignore takes precedence over the global excludesFile, so these
# re-include the source without weakening the global rule anywhere else.
!apps/api/src/credentials/
!apps/api/src/credentials/**

# Personal and generated files that were committed by accident.
#
# All three are machine-local by nature and none of them belongs in a fork:
#
#   - `.claude/settings.local.json` is per-developer tool permissions. The `*.local.*`
#     suffix is the established convention for "mine, not yours", and the copy that
#     was committed carried one machine's absolute Windows paths.
#   - `apps/web/test-results.json` is a Vitest run artifact (~50 KB) that is rewritten
#     on every test run and holds absolute paths from whoever ran it last.
#   - `__pycache__/` is CPython bytecode for `generate-icons.py`, tied to the exact
#     interpreter version that produced it.
#
# They are also the reason the template-identity guard would otherwise need three
# permanent allowlist entries: each one embeds the repository's own path or name.
.claude/settings.local.json
apps/web/test-results.json
__pycache__/
